{"name":"Winsome Orchid","hex":"#ccacc1","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"winsome","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Charming, engaging, winning; inspiring approval and trust, especially if in an innocent manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/winsome"},{"term":"orchid","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant of the orchid family (Orchidaceae), bearing unusually-shaped flowers of beautiful colours. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A light bluish-red, violet-red or purple colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a light purple colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orchid"}],"entries":[{"title":"Winsome","blocks":[{"text":"Winsome is a given name, and may refer to:"},{"items":["Winsome Andante (1993-2019), a British sport horse","Winsome Cripps (1931-1997), Australian sprinter","Winsome Douglas (1919-2016), British embroiderer and teacher","Winsome Earle-Sears, Jamaican-American politician","Winsome Evans, Australian early music specialist","Winsome Fanny Barker, South African botanist","Winsome Hall Andrew 1905-1997), Australian architect","Winsome McCaughey, Lord Mayor of Melbourne from 1988 to 1989","Winsome Pinnock, British playwright","Winsome Sears, American politician","Winsome Sinclair (1965–2024), Jamaican-born American casting director and film producer","Wincey Willis, born Florence Winsome Leighton, British television personality and weather presenter","Winsome Witch, fictional title character of an animated cartoon series"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winsome","wikidata":"Q8025976"},{"title":"Orchid","blocks":[{"text":"Orchids are plants that belong to the family Orchidaceae, a diverse and widespread group of flowering plants with blooms that are often colourful and fragrant. Orchids are cosmopolitan plants, living in diverse habitats on every continent except Antarctica. The world's richest diversity of orchid genera and species is in the tropics. Many species are epiphytes, living on trees. The flowers and their pollination mechanisms are highly specialized, attracting insect pollinators by colour, pattern, scent, pheromones, and sometimes by mimicking female insects. Orchids have very small seeds, relying on fungal partners for germination. Some orchids have no leaves, either photosynthesizing with their roots or relying entirely on fungal partners for food."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Plant_Orchid_Cymbidium_aloifolium_P1110661_05_-_cropped.jpg/330px-Plant_Orchid_Cymbidium_aloifolium_P1110661_05_-_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orchid","wikidata":"Q25308"},{"title":"Orchid (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Orchid is a bright rich purple color that resembles the color which various orchids often exhibit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Labiata.jpg/330px-Labiata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orchid_(color)","wikidata":"Q1925148"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Orchidaceae.png/500px-Orchidaceae.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Orchidaceae.png/1280px-Orchidaceae.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Orchidaceae.png/500px-Orchidaceae.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOrchidaceae.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Phaelinopsis_plant_showing_monopodial_growth.JPG/250px-Phaelinopsis_plant_showing_monopodial_growth.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_con